{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538512904,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d49f9c002T6GS9r71eW9Swf","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d490c2001Jbe6PApA8lZYn1","type":"tool","id":"call_5b1c88db66c742a7a672e14b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md, lines 1-234\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\n3: description: \"Ordered single-change tasks, grouped in waves of disjoint files, that measure the embedder's cost, make its state visible, add the plan-first doctor route, bound the prompt embedding and write the install guides.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"embedder setup and cost tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `S` is this packet's `scratch/` folder. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query over `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, as `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026 writes it. `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. No task reads holdout prompt text. The captures report holdout counts only. No task installs Ollama, pulls or deletes a model, or starts or stops the server. The values below follow the operator's answers of 2026-11-12 recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1: T006 (`E`), T007 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T008 (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), T009 (route workflow YAML), T010 (`skill-graph-db.ts`).\n35: - Wave 2: T011 (`E`), T012 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T013 (`advisor-status.ts`), T014 (`_routes.yaml`), T015 (skill-advisor presentation).\n36: - Wave 3: T016 (`E`), T017 (`advisor-status.ts`), T018 (`skill-advisor.md`), T019 (degrade test), T020 (`scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `D` regenerates).\n37: - Wave 4: T021 (`advisor-recommend.ts`), T022 (status test), T023 (`doctor-setup.yaml`), T024 (setup presentation), T025 (`doctor-install.yaml`), T026 (install presentation).\n38: - Wave 5: T027 (degrade test), T028 (route contract test), T029 (install contract test), T030 (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`), T031 (build and scan, no tracked file).\n39: - Then one at a time: T032 to T036, then T037 to T044.\n40: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n45: ## Phase 1: Setup\n46: \n47: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, tune combined 9 of 45, holdout combined 0 of 44 and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. `node $C --real-embedding | $M` prints tune combined 14 of 45 and holdout combined 2 of 44. `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n48: - [x] T002 Copy `../004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n49: - [x] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n50: - [x] T004 Save every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` (`$S/health-consumers.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"semanticLaneHealth|SemanticLaneHealth|disabledReason\" $ADV .skilled/commands/doctor --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' > $S/health-consumers.txt` exits 0 and each line is marked `reads`, `writes` or `test`.\n51: - [x] T005 Confirm phase 005 is merged before any edit to its files (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints at least one line. If it prints nothing, stop and report.\n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n57: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n58: \n59: - [x] T006 Create `E` with the server section only: read `/api/version`, `/api/tags` (the size of `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`) and `/api/ps` (loaded name, `size`, `size_vram` and `expires_at`) from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, read `ps -axo pid,rss,command` for the `ollama serve` row and the model runner row (`llama-server` or `ollama runner`), print one JSON object and exit 2 with `ollama server not answering at <url>` on stderr when `/api/version` fails (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c 'keys'` lists the server keys and exits 0, and `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E` exits 2 and prints that message.\n60: - [x] T007 In `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, add `export const PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS = 750` and race `adapter.embed([prompt], { inputType: 'query' })` against a timer that rejects with an error named `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError`. Clear the timer in a `finally`, and attach `.catch(() => undefined)` to the embed promise so a late rejection is never unhandled (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0, in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed, and `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers.\n61: - [x] T008 Add two optional fields to the semantic lane health schema. `backend` is an object with `state` in `reachable`, `unreachable`, `model_missing` or `probe_not_implemented` and a nullable `reason` string. `commandVectorCoverage` is an object with non-negative integers `embedded` and `total`. Keep the schema `.strict()` (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `rg -n \"commandVectorCoverage|probe_not_implemented\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints two lines.\n62: - [x] T009 Create the route workflow. Phase 1 probes read-only: `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Phase 2 prints the plan through the presentation contract, one line per missing step with its cost from `node $E` or the install guide and its undo. Phase 3 asks for approval and stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` on anything but approve, or stops with `STATUS=OK` after the plan under `--dry-run`. Phase 4 runs only the approved steps: `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and `ollama serve` in the background, while the Ollama install itself is only printed for the user to run. Phase 5 runs `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Phase 6 reruns the probe and renders the result, naming a daemon restart when `activeEmbedder` is null (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`). Verify: `python3 -c 'import sys,yaml; yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1]))' DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` exits 0 and `rg -n \"CANCELLED|dry_run|skill_graph_scan\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` prints at least three lines.\n63: - [x] T010 Export `readCommandEmbeddingSources` unchanged, so status can count the command entries that carry `embeddingText` (`$ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"^export function readCommandEmbeddingSources\" $ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` prints one line and `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n65: - [x] T012 In the `catch` of `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, set `disabledReason` from the error that `adapter.embed` or the deadline raised: `prompt_embedding_model_missing` for `OllamaModelNotLoadedError`, `prompt_embedding_timeout` for `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError` or `OllamaRequestTimeoutError`, `prompt_embedding_unreachable` for any other `OllamaBackendUnreachableError` and `prompt_embedding_failed` otherwise. Leave the reasons set before the embed (`database_absent`, `adapter_unavailable`, `dim_mismatch`) as they are (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"prompt_embedding_(model_missing|timeout|unreachable)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` prints three lines and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [x] T013 In `readSemanticLaneHealth`, add `commandVectorCoverage`: `embedded` counts rows of `commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim)` when that table exists and 0 otherwise, and `total` is `readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0` (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n67: - [x] T014 Add the route to the manifest after `router-reach`: `command: /doctor:skill-advisor`, `target: embedder`, `yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]`, `allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]`, `mutating: mutates`, a `gate3_location` naming the advisor database and the user's Ollama model store, the `cli_commands` T009 runs and three or more `trigger_phrases` of three or more words, such as \"set up meaning matching\", \"install the local embedder\" and \"ollama is not running for the advisor\" (`DOC/_routes.yaml`). Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n68: - [x] T015 Add the embedder blocks to the presentation contract: the probe dashboard, the plan table with columns step, cost and undo, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n -i \"embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` prints at least five lines.\n69: - [x] T016 Add the CLI section to `E`: five `X advisor_recommend` calls with distinct prompts timed end to end, printed as `cli.ms` (all five) and `cli.medianMs` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.cli'` prints five numbers and a median, and `git status --short` shows no change made by the run.\n70: - [x] T017 In `handleAdvisorStatus`, when `includeSemanticHealth` is set and the active manifest's backend is `ollama`, await `probeOllamaModel(resolveOllamaBaseUrl(), <manifest ollamaName>, 500)` and merge `backend` into `semanticLaneHealth`: `reachable` when available, `model_missing` when the reason says the model is not loaded and `unreachable` otherwise. Set `laneEnabled` to false unless `reachable`. A non-Ollama backend gets `probe_not_implemented`. Keep `readAdvisorStatus` synchronous (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n71: - [x] T018 Add the `embedder` row to the execution target table and to the `argument-hint` line (`DOC/skill-advisor.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"embedder\" DOC/skill-advisor.md` prints at least two lines.\n72: - [x] T019 Create the degrade test with the adapter, the active pointer and the read-only database mocked, and `VITEST` stubbed to `false` inside each case. Six rows: warm answer scored with a cosine, cold answer at 300 ms scored with a cosine, absent server, missing model, an answer that never arrives, which returns inside `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS` plus 100 ms, and a failure that leaves the result equal to the no-embedder result. Each failure row checks its `disabledReason` (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 6 passed.\n73: - [x] T020 Add the route's activation entry to both the `typescript` and the `python` lists, copying the shape of the `command-doctor-skill-advisor-router-reach` entries, then run `node $D` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`). Verify: `node $D --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n74: - [x] T021 Add `export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[]`, which returns a one-item array holding `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` for a reason and an empty array for null, and call it in `outputWarnings` with `getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason` read right after the scored call (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers` reports 0 failed.\n75: - [x] T022 Add status cases with fixture databases: `commandVectorCoverage` with and without a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table, and `backend` for reachable, unreachable and model missing with `probeOllamaModel` mocked (`$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and at least five more passed than before.\n76: - [x] T023 Add the sixth leg after the advisor leg: run `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only`. PASS when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0. DEGRADED otherwise, never FAIL, with repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg. Change \"five read-only legs\" to \"six\" in the file (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"Leg embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"five read-only\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints nothing.\n77: - [x] T024 Add the `embedder` leg row to the per-leg table and the `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` row to the target list (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` prints at least two lines.\n78: - [x] T025 In the checklist sentence, insert \"5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install\" before the `/doctor:setup` step, and renumber that step to 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line.\n79: - [x] T026 In the printed checklist block, insert step `5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]` with the line \"Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\" and renumber `/doctor:setup` to step 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"^5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder|^6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` prints two lines.\n80: - [x] T027 Add a seventh row to the degrade test: `semanticLaneOffWarning` returns `[\"semantic_lane_off:prompt_embedding_unreachable\"]` for that reason and `[]` for null (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed.\n81: - [x] T028 Add embedder cases to the route contract test: the route is in the manifest, its YAML stops at an approval before any `ollama pull`, `ollama serve` or `skill_graph_scan`, `--dry-run` stops after the plan and no step installs Ollama (`DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n82: - [x] T029 Update the install contract test so it expects six steps with `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` as step 5 and `/doctor:setup` as step 6 (`DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n83: - [x] T030 Add one entry for `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`: what it reads, that it writes and unloads nothing, its exit 2 and how to take a cold sample (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"measure-embedder-cost\" $ADV/scripts/README.md` prints at least one line.\n84: - [x] T031 Build and rescan so the daemon serves the new code and the route's bridge has a vector. Run `npm --prefix $ADV run build`, then `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Verify: the scan exits 0 and `sqlite3 -readonly $ADV/database/skill-graph.sqlite 'select count(*) from vec_cmd_768'` prints the same number as `jq '[.entries[] | select(.embeddingText != null)] | length' $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`.\n85: - [x] T032 Run `E` with the model loaded (`$S/cost-warm.json`). Verify: `node $E > $S/cost-warm.json` exits 0 and `jq -c '[.model.sizeBytes, .memory.serveRssKb, .memory.runnerRssKb, .warm.medianMs, .warm.p95Ms, .cli.medianMs]' $S/cost-warm.json` prints six numbers.\n86: - [x] T033 Run `E` again after the model unloaded on its own (`$S/cost-cold.json`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, without unloading it by hand. Verify: `jq -c '[.cold.firstCallMs, .idle.serveRssKb]' $S/cost-cold.json` prints two numbers.\n87: - [ ] T034 Add row 5 `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` to the Step 2 table and renumber `/doctor:setup` to 6. Add a subsection \"Meaning Matching for Commands\" to section 2 with what a user gains, the cost table from T032 and T033 with the date (disk, idle memory, loaded memory, the 5 minute unload, warm and cold latency), the fact that the step asks before it pulls the model or starts the server and never installs Ollama, and the fact that a no keeps a phrase-only install. Add a troubleshooting row for `semantic_lane_off` (`INSTALL-SKILLED.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"meaning matching|skill-advisor embedder|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least three lines and each number in the table appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n88: - [ ] T035 Add one line to section 2 saying `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default behind a yes, and a subsection to section 12 with the same cost table, the setup route and the fact that `skill_graph_scan` writes the vectors and the database is gitignored (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder|vec_cmd\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints at least two lines.\n89: - [ ] T036 Add one sentence to section 12 saying `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes the hf-local server only and `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"includeEmbeddingsHealth\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints one line that names hf-local.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: ## Phase 3: Verification\n96: \n97: - [x] T037 Run the typecheck and the suite. Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `npm --prefix $ADV test` reports 0 failed.\n98: - [x] T038 Rerun the default capture, the floor and the rollup. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n99: - [x] T039 Rerun the real-embedding capture and the phrase-reach probe (`$S/real-embedding-after.json`). Verify: `node $C --real-embedding > $S/real-embedding-after.json` exits 0, `$M` over it prints tune combined 14 of 45, holdout combined 2 of 44, typed 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` exits 0.\n100: - [x] T040 Run the doctor suites. Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed and `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n101: - [x] T041 Run `$S/hook-latency.mjs` three times (`$S/hook-latency-after-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: the middle median is at most 25 ms over the T002 middle median and the middle p95 at most 40 ms over the T002 middle p95.\n102: - [x] T042 Run the new setup leg's command once with the server running (`$S/setup-leg.txt`). Verify: `jq -c '.data.semanticLaneHealth | [.laneEnabled, .backend.state, .commandVectorCoverage.embedded > 0]'` over its output prints `[true,\"reachable\",true]`.\n103: - [x] T043 Run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder --dry-run` in a session (`$S/route-dry-run.txt`). Verify: the transcript shows the plan with a cost and an undo per step and `STATUS=OK`, `git status --short` is unchanged and the database's `stat -f %m` is unchanged.\n104: - [ ] T044 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n105: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n110: ## Completion Criteria\n111: \n112: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n113: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n114: - [ ] `$S/cost-warm.json` and `$S/cost-cold.json` hold the numbers the install guides print, and the degrade test reports 7 passed\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n120: ## Cross-References\n121: \n122: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n123: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n124: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n125: - **Skill-level embedding owner**: `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement/spec.md`\n126: - **Command vectors**: `../004-command-meaning-matching/implementation-summary.md`\n127: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## Verification Checklist\n132: \n133: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n134: ## Verification Protocol\n135: \n136: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n137: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n138: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n139: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n140: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n141: \n142: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A route step that runs before the approval blocks the phase.\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n148: ## Pre-Implementation\n149: \n150: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n151: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Phase 005 is merged: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line (T005).\n152: - [x] CHK-003 [P1] The four planning questions have an operator answer. Evidence: 2026-11-12, recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n153: - [ ] CHK-004 [P1] `$S/cold-after-abort.txt` records whether a load continues after the client gives up (T003).\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n159: ## Code Quality\n160: \n161: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n162: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number or a task id: `rg -n \"T0[0-9]{2}|REQ-0|specs/\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n163: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] No file under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared` changed: `git diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared` prints nothing.\n164: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The deadline timer is cleared and the late embed rejection is caught (T007).\n165: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n166: \n167: ---\n168: \n169: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n170: ## Testing Checklist\n171: \n172: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The degrade test reports 7 passed (T027).\n173: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The captures, the floor and the rollup are unchanged (T038, T039).\n174: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The route contract test passes and no step runs before the approval (T028).\n175: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The hook stays inside the budget (T041).\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n181: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: the prompt embedding deadline is set by a shared adapter that the hook budget never sees.\n184: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` is listed in `$S/health-consumers.txt` (T004).\n185: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of `outputWarnings` output are checked: `rg -n \"warnings\" $ADV/tests/handlers` cases still pass (T037).\n186: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The six matrix rows in `plan.md` are listed in the degrade test header.\n187: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The suite passes with `VITEST` set, and the degrade test stubs it off per case.\n188: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n194: ## Security\n195: \n196: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] The route runs no `ollama pull`, `ollama serve` or scan before the approval (T028).\n197: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No step installs Ollama. The install command is printed only: `rg -n \"brew install|curl .*install\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` shows it only inside a print step.\n198: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The script and the probe call only `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n204: ## Documentation\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same deadline and the same answers to the four questions.\n207: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Every cost number in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] `$ADV/scripts/README.md` names the script and its exit 2.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n214: ## File Organization\n215: \n216: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Timing runs, cost output and transcripts live in `scratch/` only.\n217: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n218: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n219: \n220: ---\n221: \n222: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n223: ## Verification Summary\n224: \n225: | Category | Total | Verified |\n226: |----------|-------|----------|\n227: | P0 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n228: | P1 Items | 12 | 1/12 |\n229: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n230: \n231: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n233: \n234: ---","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md, lines 1-234\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\"\n3: description: \"Ordered single-change tasks, grouped in waves of disjoint files, that measure the embedder's cost, make its state visible, add the plan-first doctor route, bound the prompt embedding and write the install guides.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"embedder setup and cost tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 8: embedder-setup-and-cost\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: \n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n27: \n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `DOC` is `.skilled/commands/doctor`. `S` is this packet's `scratch/` folder. `X` is `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`. `E` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`. `C` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `M` is `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .attachedMetrics.plain, .metrics.false_offer'`. `P` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`. `R` is the phase 002 rollup query over `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, as `../002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/tasks.md` T026 writes it. `D` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`.\n29: \n30: Each task is one change to the files it names, small enough for a worker with a short brief. No task reads holdout prompt text. The captures report holdout counts only. No task installs Ollama, pulls or deletes a model, or starts or stops the server. The values below follow the operator's answers of 2026-11-12 recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n31: \n32: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel.\n33: - Wave 0: T001, T002, T003, T004, T005. Read-only setup.\n34: - Wave 1: T006 (`E`), T007 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T008 (`advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), T009 (route workflow YAML), T010 (`skill-graph-db.ts`).\n35: - Wave 2: T011 (`E`), T012 (`semantic-shadow.ts`), T013 (`advisor-status.ts`), T014 (`_routes.yaml`), T015 (skill-advisor presentation).\n36: - Wave 3: T016 (`E`), T017 (`advisor-status.ts`), T018 (`skill-advisor.md`), T019 (degrade test), T020 (`scoring-compatibility.json` and the files `D` regenerates).\n37: - Wave 4: T021 (`advisor-recommend.ts`), T022 (status test), T023 (`doctor-setup.yaml`), T024 (setup presentation), T025 (`doctor-install.yaml`), T026 (install presentation).\n38: - Wave 5: T027 (degrade test), T028 (route contract test), T029 (install contract test), T030 (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`), T031 (build and scan, no tracked file).\n39: - Then one at a time: T032 to T036, then T037 to T044.\n40: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n45: ## Phase 1: Setup\n46: \n47: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$S/before.txt`). Verify: `node $C | $M` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, tune combined 9 of 45, holdout combined 0 of 44 and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`. `node $C --real-embedding | $M` prints tune combined 14 of 45 and holdout combined 2 of 44. `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n48: - [x] T002 Copy `../004-command-meaning-matching/scratch/hook-latency.mjs` to `$S/hook-latency.mjs` and run it three times (`$S/hook-latency-before-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: `jq -c '[.n,.medianMs,.p95Ms]'` on each file prints 44 and two numbers.\n49: - [x] T003 Record whether Ollama keeps loading the model after a client gives up (`$S/cold-after-abort.txt`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, then run `curl -s -m 0.05 localhost:11434/api/embed -d '{\"model\":\"nomic-embed-text:v1.5\",\"input\":\"x\"}'; sleep 3; curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq -r '.models[].name'`. Verify: the file holds the last command's output and one line saying whether it lists `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`.\n50: - [x] T004 Save every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` (`$S/health-consumers.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"semanticLaneHealth|SemanticLaneHealth|disabledReason\" $ADV .skilled/commands/doctor --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' > $S/health-consumers.txt` exits 0 and each line is marked `reads`, `writes` or `test`.\n51: - [x] T005 Confirm phase 005 is merged before any edit to its files (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints at least one line. If it prints nothing, stop and report.\n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n57: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n58: \n59: - [x] T006 Create `E` with the server section only: read `/api/version`, `/api/tags` (the size of `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`) and `/api/ps` (loaded name, `size`, `size_vram` and `expires_at`) from `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, read `ps -axo pid,rss,command` for the `ollama serve` row and the model runner row (`llama-server` or `ollama runner`), print one JSON object and exit 2 with `ollama server not answering at <url>` on stderr when `/api/version` fails (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c 'keys'` lists the server keys and exits 0, and `OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9 node $E` exits 2 and prints that message.\n60: - [x] T007 In `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, add `export const PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS = 750` and race `adapter.embed([prompt], { inputType: 'query' })` against a timer that rejects with an error named `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError`. Clear the timer in a `finally`, and attach `.catch(() => undefined)` to the embed promise so a late rejection is never unhandled (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0, in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed, and `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers.\n61: - [x] T008 Add two optional fields to the semantic lane health schema. `backend` is an object with `state` in `reachable`, `unreachable`, `model_missing` or `probe_not_implemented` and a nullable `reason` string. `commandVectorCoverage` is an object with non-negative integers `embedded` and `total`. Keep the schema `.strict()` (`$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `rg -n \"commandVectorCoverage|probe_not_implemented\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints two lines.\n62: - [x] T009 Create the route workflow. Phase 1 probes read-only: `command -v ollama`, `/api/version`, `/api/tags` and `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --warm-only`. Phase 2 prints the plan through the presentation contract, one line per missing step with its cost from `node $E` or the install guide and its undo. Phase 3 asks for approval and stops with `STATUS=CANCELLED` on anything but approve, or stops with `STATUS=OK` after the plan under `--dry-run`. Phase 4 runs only the approved steps: `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` and `ollama serve` in the background, while the Ollama install itself is only printed for the user to run. Phase 5 runs `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Phase 6 reruns the probe and renders the result, naming a daemon restart when `activeEmbedder` is null (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`). Verify: `python3 -c 'import sys,yaml; yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1]))' DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` exits 0 and `rg -n \"CANCELLED|dry_run|skill_graph_scan\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` prints at least three lines.\n63: - [x] T010 Export `readCommandEmbeddingSources` unchanged, so status can count the command entries that carry `embeddingText` (`$ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"^export function readCommandEmbeddingSources\" $ADV/lib/skill-graph/skill-graph-db.ts` prints one line and `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n64: - [x] T011 Add the embedding section to `E`: 30 query embeddings through the shared `OllamaAdapter` from `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/dist/embeddings/adapters/ollama.js` with the `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` manifest from `registry.js`, printed as `warm.medianMs` and `warm.p95Ms`. When `/api/ps` listed no model before the first call, record that first call as `cold.firstCallMs` and the `ollama serve` resident memory as `idle.serveRssKb`. Otherwise print `cold: null` with the reason `model already loaded` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.warm, .cold'` prints `n` 30, a median, a p95 and either `null` or a number.\n65: - [x] T012 In the `catch` of `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, set `disabledReason` from the error that `adapter.embed` or the deadline raised: `prompt_embedding_model_missing` for `OllamaModelNotLoadedError`, `prompt_embedding_timeout` for `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError` or `OllamaRequestTimeoutError`, `prompt_embedding_unreachable` for any other `OllamaBackendUnreachableError` and `prompt_embedding_failed` otherwise. Leave the reasons set before the embed (`database_absent`, `adapter_unavailable`, `dim_mismatch`) as they are (`$ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`). Verify: `rg -n \"prompt_embedding_(model_missing|timeout|unreachable)\" $ADV/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts` prints three lines and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/scorer` reports 0 failed.\n66: - [x] T013 In `readSemanticLaneHealth`, add `commandVectorCoverage`: `embedded` counts rows of `commandVecTableNameForDim(activeDim)` when that table exists and 0 otherwise, and `total` is `readCommandEmbeddingSources()?.length ?? 0` (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n67: - [x] T014 Add the route to the manifest after `router-reach`: `command: /doctor:skill-advisor`, `target: embedder`, `yaml: doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, `setup_vars: [execution_mode, dry_run]`, `allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\"]`, `mutating: mutates`, a `gate3_location` naming the advisor database and the user's Ollama model store, the `cli_commands` T009 runs and three or more `trigger_phrases` of three or more words, such as \"set up meaning matching\", \"install the local embedder\" and \"ollama is not running for the advisor\" (`DOC/_routes.yaml`). Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n68: - [x] T015 Add the embedder blocks to the presentation contract: the probe dashboard, the plan table with columns step, cost and undo, the approval prompt, the dry-run result and the final result (`DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n -i \"embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` prints at least five lines.\n69: - [x] T016 Add the CLI section to `E`: five `X advisor_recommend` calls with distinct prompts timed end to end, printed as `cli.ms` (all five) and `cli.medianMs` (`E`). Verify: `node $E | jq -c '.cli'` prints five numbers and a median, and `git status --short` shows no change made by the run.\n70: - [x] T017 In `handleAdvisorStatus`, when `includeSemanticHealth` is set and the active manifest's backend is `ollama`, await `probeOllamaModel(resolveOllamaBaseUrl(), <manifest ollamaName>, 500)` and merge `backend` into `semanticLaneHealth`: `reachable` when available, `model_missing` when the reason says the model is not loaded and `unreachable` otherwise. Set `laneEnabled` to false unless `reachable`. A non-Ollama backend gets `probe_not_implemented`. Keep `readAdvisorStatus` synchronous (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`). Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. The live value is checked in T042.\n71: - [x] T018 Add the `embedder` row to the execution target table and to the `argument-hint` line (`DOC/skill-advisor.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"embedder\" DOC/skill-advisor.md` prints at least two lines.\n72: - [x] T019 Create the degrade test with the adapter, the active pointer and the read-only database mocked, and `VITEST` stubbed to `false` inside each case. Six rows: warm answer scored with a cosine, cold answer at 300 ms scored with a cosine, absent server, missing model, an answer that never arrives, which returns inside `PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS` plus 100 ms, and a failure that leaves the result equal to the no-embedder result. Each failure row checks its `disabledReason` (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 6 passed.\n73: - [x] T020 Add the route's activation entry to both the `typescript` and the `python` lists, copying the shape of the `command-doctor-skill-advisor-router-reach` entries, then run `node $D` (`$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json`). Verify: `node $D --check` prints `\"status\": \"fresh\"` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n74: - [x] T021 Add `export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[]`, which returns a one-item array holding `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` for a reason and an empty array for null, and call it in `outputWarnings` with `getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason` read right after the scored call (`$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers` reports 0 failed.\n75: - [x] T022 Add status cases with fixture databases: `commandVectorCoverage` with and without a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table, and `backend` for reachable, unreachable and model missing with `probeOllamaModel` mocked (`$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and at least five more passed than before.\n76: - [x] T023 Add the sixth leg after the advisor leg: run `X advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only`. PASS when `laneEnabled` is true and `commandVectorCoverage.embedded` is above 0. DEGRADED otherwise, never FAIL, with repair `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg. Change \"five read-only legs\" to \"six\" in the file (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"Leg embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"five read-only\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup.yaml` prints nothing.\n77: - [x] T024 Add the `embedder` leg row to the per-leg table and the `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` row to the target list (`DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt` prints at least two lines.\n78: - [x] T025 In the checklist sentence, insert \"5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder, from inside the target repo, to set up meaning matching for commands. It shows its cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server, and a no leaves a phrase-only install\" before the `/doctor:setup` step, and renumber that step to 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml`). Verify: `rg -n \"5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line and `rg -n \"6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install.yaml` prints one line.\n79: - [x] T026 In the printed checklist block, insert step `5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]` with the line \"Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\" and renumber `/doctor:setup` to step 6 (`DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt`). Verify: `rg -n \"^5\\) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder|^6\\) /doctor:setup\" DOC/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt` prints two lines.\n80: - [x] T027 Add a seventh row to the degrade test: `semanticLaneOffWarning` returns `[\"semantic_lane_off:prompt_embedding_unreachable\"]` for that reason and `[]` for null (`$ADV/tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts`). Verify: in `$ADV` `npx vitest run tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` reports 7 passed.\n81: - [x] T028 Add embedder cases to the route contract test: the route is in the manifest, its YAML stops at an approval before any `ollama pull`, `ollama serve` or `skill_graph_scan`, `--dry-run` stops after the plan and no step installs Ollama (`DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/skill-advisor-route-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n82: - [x] T029 Update the install contract test so it expects six steps with `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` as step 5 and `/doctor:setup` as step 6 (`DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs`). Verify: `node DOC/scripts/tests/doctor-install-contract.test.cjs` exits 0.\n83: - [x] T030 Add one entry for `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`: what it reads, that it writes and unloads nothing, its exit 2 and how to take a cold sample (`$ADV/scripts/README.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"measure-embedder-cost\" $ADV/scripts/README.md` prints at least one line.\n84: - [x] T031 Build and rescan so the daemon serves the new code and the route's bridge has a vector. Run `npm --prefix $ADV run build`, then `X skill_graph_scan --trusted --format json`. Verify: the scan exits 0 and `sqlite3 -readonly $ADV/database/skill-graph.sqlite 'select count(*) from vec_cmd_768'` prints the same number as `jq '[.entries[] | select(.embeddingText != null)] | length' $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`.\n85: - [x] T032 Run `E` with the model loaded (`$S/cost-warm.json`). Verify: `node $E > $S/cost-warm.json` exits 0 and `jq -c '[.model.sizeBytes, .memory.serveRssKb, .memory.runnerRssKb, .warm.medianMs, .warm.p95Ms, .cli.medianMs]' $S/cost-warm.json` prints six numbers.\n86: - [x] T033 Run `E` again after the model unloaded on its own (`$S/cost-cold.json`). Wait until `curl -s localhost:11434/api/ps | jq '.models | length'` prints 0, without unloading it by hand. Verify: `jq -c '[.cold.firstCallMs, .idle.serveRssKb]' $S/cost-cold.json` prints two numbers.\n87: - [ ] T034 Add row 5 `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` to the Step 2 table and renumber `/doctor:setup` to 6. Add a subsection \"Meaning Matching for Commands\" to section 2 with what a user gains, the cost table from T032 and T033 with the date (disk, idle memory, loaded memory, the 5 minute unload, warm and cold latency), the fact that the step asks before it pulls the model or starts the server and never installs Ollama, and the fact that a no keeps a phrase-only install. Add a troubleshooting row for `semantic_lane_off` (`INSTALL-SKILLED.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"meaning matching|skill-advisor embedder|semantic_lane_off\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` prints at least three lines and each number in the table appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n88: - [ ] T035 Add one line to section 2 saying `/doctor:install` sets up the embedder by default behind a yes, and a subsection to section 12 with the same cost table, the setup route and the fact that `skill_graph_scan` writes the vectors and the database is gitignored (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"skill-advisor embedder|vec_cmd\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints at least two lines.\n89: - [ ] T036 Add one sentence to section 12 saying `includeEmbeddingsHealth` probes the hf-local server only and `includeSemanticHealth` reports the active embedder (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md`). Verify: `rg -n \"includeEmbeddingsHealth\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md` prints one line that names hf-local.\n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n95: ## Phase 3: Verification\n96: \n97: - [x] T037 Run the typecheck and the suite. Verify: `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0 and `npm --prefix $ADV test` reports 0 failed.\n98: - [x] T038 Rerun the default capture, the floor and the rollup. Verify: `node $C | $M` prints the T001 numbers, `$P` prints `[159,50,20,5]` and `R` prints `{\"ask\":17,\"run\":7,\"start\":20}`.\n99: - [x] T039 Rerun the real-embedding capture and the phrase-reach probe (`$S/real-embedding-after.json`). Verify: `node $C --real-embedding > $S/real-embedding-after.json` exits 0, `$M` over it prints tune combined 14 of 45, holdout combined 2 of 44, typed 24 of 44 and false offers 0 of 35, and `node DOC/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs` exits 0.\n100: - [x] T040 Run the doctor suites. Verify: `bash DOC/scripts/tests/run-all.sh` reports 0 failed and `bash DOC/scripts/route-validate.sh` exits 0.\n101: - [x] T041 Run `$S/hook-latency.mjs` three times (`$S/hook-latency-after-{1,2,3}.json`). Verify: the middle median is at most 25 ms over the T002 middle median and the middle p95 at most 40 ms over the T002 middle p95.\n102: - [x] T042 Run the new setup leg's command once with the server running (`$S/setup-leg.txt`). Verify: `jq -c '.data.semanticLaneHealth | [.laneEnabled, .backend.state, .commandVectorCoverage.embedded > 0]'` over its output prints `[true,\"reachable\",true]`.\n103: - [x] T043 Run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder --dry-run` in a session (`$S/route-dry-run.txt`). Verify: the transcript shows the plan with a cost and an undo per step and `STATUS=OK`, `git status --short` is unchanged and the database's `stat -f %m` is unchanged.\n104: - [ ] T044 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n105: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n110: ## Completion Criteria\n111: \n112: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n113: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n114: - [ ] `$S/cost-warm.json` and `$S/cost-cold.json` hold the numbers the install guides print, and the degrade test reports 7 passed\n115: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n120: ## Cross-References\n121: \n122: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n123: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n124: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n125: - **Skill-level embedding owner**: `../../001-semantic-lane-enablement/spec.md`\n126: - **Command vectors**: `../004-command-meaning-matching/implementation-summary.md`\n127: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## Verification Checklist\n132: \n133: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n134: ## Verification Protocol\n135: \n136: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n137: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n138: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n139: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n140: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n141: \n142: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A route step that runs before the approval blocks the phase.\n143: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n144: \n145: ---\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n148: ## Pre-Implementation\n149: \n150: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers are in `$S/before.txt` (T001).\n151: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Phase 005 is merged: `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" $ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line (T005).\n152: - [x] CHK-003 [P1] The four planning questions have an operator answer. Evidence: 2026-11-12, recorded in `spec.md` section 10.\n153: - [ ] CHK-004 [P1] `$S/cold-after-abort.txt` records whether a load continues after the client gives up (T003).\n154: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n159: ## Code Quality\n160: \n161: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` exits 0.\n162: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number or a task id: `rg -n \"T0[0-9]{2}|REQ-0|specs/\" <changed files>` prints nothing.\n163: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] No file under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared` changed: `git diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared` prints nothing.\n164: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The deadline timer is cleared and the late embed rejection is caught (T007).\n165: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n166: \n167: ---\n168: \n169: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n170: ## Testing Checklist\n171: \n172: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] The degrade test reports 7 passed (T027).\n173: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The captures, the floor and the rollup are unchanged (T038, T039).\n174: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The route contract test passes and no step runs before the approval (T028).\n175: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The hook stays inside the budget (T041).\n176: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n177: \n178: ---\n179: \n180: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n181: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n182: \n183: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `cross-consumer`: the prompt embedding deadline is set by a shared adapter that the hook budget never sees.\n184: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the semantic lane health and of `disabledReason` is listed in `$S/health-consumers.txt` (T004).\n185: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumers of `outputWarnings` output are checked: `rg -n \"warnings\" $ADV/tests/handlers` cases still pass (T037).\n186: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The six matrix rows in `plan.md` are listed in the degrade test header.\n187: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The suite passes with `VITEST` set, and the degrade test stubs it off per case.\n188: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n189: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n190: \n191: ---\n192: \n193: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n194: ## Security\n195: \n196: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] The route runs no `ollama pull`, `ollama serve` or scan before the approval (T028).\n197: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No step installs Ollama. The install command is printed only: `rg -n \"brew install|curl .*install\" DOC/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` shows it only inside a print step.\n198: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The script and the probe call only `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:11434`.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n204: ## Documentation\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same deadline and the same answers to the four questions.\n207: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Every cost number in `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` and `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` appears in `$S/cost-warm.json` or `$S/cost-cold.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-042 [P2] `$ADV/scripts/README.md` names the script and its exit 2.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n214: ## File Organization\n215: \n216: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Timing runs, cost output and transcripts live in `scratch/` only.\n217: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds only the evidence files the summary cites at completion.\n218: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n219: \n220: ---\n221: \n222: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n223: ## Verification Summary\n224: \n225: | Category | Total | Verified |\n226: |----------|-------|----------|\n227: | P0 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n228: | P1 Items | 12 | 1/12 |\n229: | P2 Items | 1 | 0/1 |\n230: \n231: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-12\n232: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n233: \n234: ---"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538512284,"end":1794538512904}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794538514717,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"id":"prt_1d2d4a91d001KLZTrDyhEXUMKh","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d490c2001Jbe6PApA8lZYn1","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a6679670c5cc6f61baa605e1c3425447e7ded983","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":17167,"output":103,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":384,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794538518555,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"id":"prt_1d2d4b81b001aJa8yD8wRNJ00t","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d4a922001ANWbNghFUayWba","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9bdd175438a6dac89a684fdd3857f73ac96a46eb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538523547,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d4c880002gXMIaazgx3qbR3","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d4a922001ANWbNghFUayWba","type":"tool","id":"call_a3799a869dbe4ea5927c3c49","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 1-337\n1: # Install Skilled\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: This guide installs Skilled and then sets it up in your own project repositories. Section 2 installs and checks a Skilled checkout. Sections 3 and 4 bring that checkout into a project, by linking it or by copying it in.\n6: \n7: From section 3 on, you run each step as a `/doctor` command from the `system-skilled-doctor` skill. A command that writes shows you a plan first and waits for your yes.\n8: \n9: ### Link or Copy\n10: \n11: You can set up a project in one of two ways. Pick one per project.\n12: \n13: | | Link | Copy |\n14: | --- | --- | --- |\n15: | **How it works** | Your project links to your Skilled checkout | Your project commits its own copy of Skilled |\n16: | **Updates** | One `git pull` in the checkout updates every linked project | You re-pin the copy: move it from the commit it came from to a newer one |\n17: | **Your changes** | Live in your project's own files, next to the links | Live in an overlay folder that goes back on the copy after each update |\n18: | **Teammates** | Each one keeps their own Skilled checkout | Everyone gets Skilled from the project repo |\n19: | **Choose it when** | You work alone, or every teammate keeps a checkout | The team needs one pinned version, or you change Skilled's own files |\n20: \n21: Linking is simpler. Choose a copy only when you need one of its two reasons.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. INSTALL A SKILLED CHECKOUT\n26: \n27: ### Prerequisites\n28: \n29: You need Node.js 24, `npm`, `git` and a POSIX shell. Node 24 is the one version every part of the framework accepts.\n30: \n31: ### Clone and Build\n32: \n33: Clone the repository and step into it:\n34: \n35: ```bash\n36: git clone https://github.com/MichelKerkmeester/skilled-agent-harness_spec-driven-loops.git\n37: cd skilled-agent-harness_spec-driven-loops\n38: ```\n39: \n40: Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n41: \n42: ```bash\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Then build the Skill Advisor. Its build uses the Spec Kit's TypeScript compiler, so it comes second. The last command checks the advisor's CLI. `list-tools` answers offline, with no daemon running.\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: ### Add Code Mode\n72: \n73: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n74: \n75: ```\n76: /doctor:mcp install\n77: ```\n78: \n79: It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n80: \n81: To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n82: \n83: ### Git Hooks\n84: \n85: The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n86: \n87: Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\n88: \n89: ---\n90: \n91: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n92: \n93: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n94: \n95: Open your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n96: \n97: ```\n98: /doctor:install\n99: ```\n100: \n101: It asks four questions in one prompt:\n102: \n103: 1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n104: 2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n105: 3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n106: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n107: \n108: <!-- readme-check\n109: allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n110: -->\n111: \n112: The guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n113: \n114: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n115: \n116: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n117: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n118: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n119: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n120: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n121: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n122: | 5 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n123: \n124: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n125: \n126: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n127: \n128: ```\n129: /doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n130: ```\n131: \n132: Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n133: \n134: ### What Gets Linked\n135: \n136: - **Always:** `.skilled`.\n137: - **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n138: - **On request:** `--include` takes `repo-rules`, `github`, `utcp` or `env`. They add the `repo-rules` folder, `.github`, `.utcp_config.json` and `.env`.\n139: - **Secrets:** linking `.env` shares the checkout's secrets with every tool in the project. The plan warns you before you approve it.\n140: \n141: The link shape decides how each folder is linked:\n142: \n143: - **`whole`:** each folder becomes one link to the checkout where it can.\n144: - **`merge`:** the folder stays a real folder, and each entry inside it becomes its own link.\n145: - **`auto`:** picks per folder, as described below.\n146: \n147: With `auto`, a folder your project already has stays a real folder. Each entry inside it becomes its own link, and your own files there stay untouched.\n148: \n149: A folder your project lacks becomes one link. The exception is a folder that holds a link to a sibling folder, such as `.skilled` (its `specs` link) or `.claude` (its `skills` link). The engine builds that folder entry by entry instead.\n150: \n151: ### Keep the Links Out of Git\n152: \n153: Most links point at your machine's checkout, so never commit them. `link` writes an ignore line for each of those to `.git/info/exclude`. Git reads that file but never commits it. Pass `--ignore gitignore` to write `.gitignore` instead.\n154: \n155: One link is different. When your project has its own `specs/` folder, `.skilled/specs` links to it with a relative path. That link works on any machine, so it receives no ignore line and you can commit it.\n156: \n157: ### Undo a Link\n158: \n159: Each `link` run ends by printing its undo command:\n160: \n161: ```\n162: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <run dir> --dry-run\n163: ```\n164: \n165: `/doctor:symlink unlink --run <run dir>` does the same. Drop `--dry-run` to run it for real. Unlink removes only what that run created. It restores only what that run replaced, and it removes the run's ignore lines. After several `link` runs, undo the newest first.\n166: \n167: > **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\n168: \n169: ---\n170: \n171: ## 4. COPY IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n172: \n173: A re-pin replaces your copy whole with a newer commit. A change you made to the copy would be lost, so each change lives in an overlay instead. An overlay is a file in your project's overlay folder. `/doctor:overlay` applies it on top of the copy.\n174: \n175: <!-- readme-check\n176: allow-ref overlay-manifest.json | the manifest inside the overlay folder of a project that copies Skilled in\n177: allow-ref skilled-overlays/overlay-manifest.json | the manifest path the engine names in its error, in a project that copies Skilled in\n178: allow-ref skilled-overlays/ | the overlay folder in a project that copies Skilled in, which this checkout does not ship\n179: allow-ref .skilled-overlays.json | the optional overlay folder setting in a project that copies Skilled in, which this checkout does not ship\n180: -->\n181: \n182: ### Step 1: Create the Copy\n183: \n184: Export `.skilled` and the runtime folders you use from one commit of your checkout:\n185: \n186: ```bash\n187: cd /path/to/skilled\n188: git archive <commit> .skilled .claude .opencode | tar -x -C /path/to/your-project\n189: ```\n190: \n191: Commit the result in your project. Note the commit you exported. That commit is your pin.\n192: \n193: ### Step 2: Create the Overlay Folder\n194: \n195: The engine looks for `skilled-overlays/` at the root of your project. To use another folder, add `.skilled-overlays.json` at the root, for example `{ \"overlayDir\": \"my-overlays\" }`.\n196: \n197: The folder holds `overlay-manifest.json` and your overlay files. This manifest replaces one upstream file and adds a folder of team commands:\n198: \n199: ```json\n200: {\n201:   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n202:   \"pin\": { \"upstream\": \"skilled\", \"commit\": \"<the commit you exported>\" },\n203:   \"layoutLinks\": [],\n204:   \"overlays\": [\n205:     {\n206:       \"id\": \"commit-template\",\n207:       \"scope\": \"file\",\n208:       \"source\": \"sk-git/commit-message-template.md\",\n209:       \"destination\": \".skilled/skills/sk-git/assets/commit-message-template.md\"\n210:     },\n211:     {\n212:       \"id\": \"team-commands\",\n213:       \"scope\": \"directory\",\n214:       \"source\": \"team-commands\",\n215:       \"destination\": \".skilled/commands/team\"\n216:     }\n217:   ],\n218:   \"regenerate\": [],\n219:   \"verifyGenerated\": []\n220: }\n221: ```\n222: \n223: - **`source`:** where your version lives, inside the overlay folder.\n224: - **`destination`:** the path in the copy that the overlay owns.\n225: \n226: Save your version of each file at its `source` path.\n227: \n228: ### Overlay Types\n229: \n230: | `scope` | What the overlay does |\n231: | --- | --- |\n232: | `file` | Replaces one file with your version |\n233: | `directory` | Keeps a folder equal to your folder |\n234: | `marked-section` | Keeps your block between two marker lines in an upstream file |\n235: | `json-entry` | Changes named keys in an upstream JSON file |\n236: | `skill-root` | Replaces a whole skill folder with yours |\n237: | `remove-root` | Removes named upstream paths from the copy |\n238: \n239: Most projects need only `file` and `directory`. The [overlays reference](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md) covers the rest, plus the optional `regenerate`, `verifyGenerated` and `repin` blocks.\n240: \n241: ### Step 3: Apply the Overlays\n242: \n243: Check what is out of sync:\n244: \n245: ```\n246: /doctor:overlay status\n247: ```\n248: \n249: A new overlay reads `overlay-edited`, because the copy does not have it yet. Apply it:\n250: \n251: ```\n252: /doctor:overlay apply\n253: ```\n254: \n255: `apply` shows the status report as its plan and writes after your yes. Run `status` again. It now ends with `RESULT: PASSED`. Commit the overlay folder and the copy together.\n256: \n257: Running `apply` a second time changes nothing.\n258: \n259: ### Change an Overlay\n260: \n261: Edit the file in the overlay folder, never in the copy. Then run `apply`.\n262: \n263: Someone may still edit the copy directly. `status` then reports the file as `live-edited`, and `apply` refuses to write. Move the edit into its overlay:\n264: \n265: ```\n266: /doctor:overlay apply --capture <path>\n267: ```\n268: \n269: An AI agent is stopped sooner. The `overlay-guard` hook refuses an agent's edit to a file an overlay owns. It names the overlay file to edit instead.\n270: \n271: ### Step 4: Re-Pin to a Newer Commit\n272: \n273: A re-pin moves your copy to a newer commit and applies your overlays again. It reads from your Skilled checkout, which must hold both your pin and the new commit:\n274: \n275: ```\n276: /doctor:overlay repin --upstream /path/to/skilled --to <new commit>\n277: ```\n278: \n279: 1. **It stages first.** It builds the result in a temporary folder and leaves your project alone. The report lists the paths it will copy and delete, any blocked overlays and any overlays that now equal upstream.\n280: 2. **You fix the report.** Update each blocked overlay to match the new upstream file. Remove each overlay that now equals upstream. Run the command again.\n281: 3. **You approve.** The live run backs up every path it touches. Then it copies, moves the pin and applies the overlays.\n282: 4. **It checks the result.** The run ends with `RESULT: PASSED` and the new pin in your manifest.\n283: \n284: A re-pin copies `.skilled` and the runtime folders. It never copies a root file such as `AGENTS.md`, so your project's version survives. Each upstream change it skips prints as a `not-copied` line. Copy those over by hand if you want them. A top-level link, such as `specs`, is skipped without a line.\n285: \n286: A re-pin refuses to start when someone edited a file in place that no overlay owns, because the new copy would erase that edit. The refusal names the file. Move the edit into an overlay or add the path to the manifest's `repin.exclude` list. You can also restore the file from your pin.\n287: \n288: ### Undo a Re-Pin\n289: \n290: Each live run saves a backup in `skilled-overlays/repin-runs/<run-id>/` and prints the run id. Undo it with:\n291: \n292: ```\n293: /doctor:overlay repin --rollback <run-id>\n294: ```\n295: \n296: Rollback restores every backed-up file byte for byte. It removes the files the run added and sets the old pin back. Run `/doctor:overlay status` afterwards to confirm.\n297: \n298: ### Bring an Existing Overlay Folder\n299: \n300: Already keep overlays with a script of your own? The engine reads the same manifest and state files, so the folder stays where it is. Name it in `.skilled-overlays.json` and run `status`. Each line names its fix. The overlays reference has the full [adoption steps](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md#6-adopting-the-engine-with-existing-overlays).\n301: \n302: ---\n303: \n304: ## 5. KEEP IT HEALTHY\n305: \n306: | When | Linked project | Copied project |\n307: | --- | --- | --- |\n308: | **After a `git pull` in the checkout** | Run `/doctor:symlink check --root <dir>`. Run `link` again if it lists missing entries | No action until you re-pin |\n309: | **To adopt a new Skilled release** | The `git pull` already adopted it | Run `/doctor:overlay repin` |\n310: | **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n311: | **To find the right command** | Run `/doctor:helper` and describe the problem | Same as linked |\n312: \n313: ---\n314: \n315: ## 6. TROUBLESHOOTING\n316: \n317: | You see | Cause | Fix |\n318: | --- | --- | --- |\n319: | `partial-merge` in `/doctor:symlink check` | The checkout gained entries since your last `link` | Run `link` again |\n320: | `no overlay manifest at skilled-overlays/overlay-manifest.json` | The engine found no overlay folder | Create one (section 4, step 2), or name yours in `.skilled-overlays.json` |\n321: | `overlay-edited` | An overlay changed and the copy lags behind | Run `/doctor:overlay apply` |\n322: | `live-edited` | Someone edited the copy directly | Run `/doctor:overlay apply --capture <path>` |\n323: | `both-changed` | The overlay and the copy both changed since the last apply | Read both, update the overlay by hand and run `status` again |\n324: | `upstream-moved` | The pin moved, and the file matches neither the old copy nor your overlay | Update the overlay to fit the new upstream file and run `status` again |\n325: | `refusing to inspect a protected path` | An overlay walks a file with `token` in its name | Add that file to the overlay's `protectedPaths`, as the line says |\n326: | `refuse: unowned <path> differs from the old pin` | Someone edited a file in place that no overlay owns | Move the edit into an overlay, or restore the file from your pin |\n327: | A held `.build-lock` | Another `apply` is running, or one crashed | Once no run is active, delete the lock file the message names |\n328: \n329: ---\n330: \n331: ## 7. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n332: \n333: - [system-skilled-doctor README](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/README.md): every doctor command in this guide.\n334: - [Overlays reference](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md): sync states, refusals, re-pins and adoption in full.\n335: - [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n336: - [Root README](README.md): what Skilled is and what each part does.\n337: - [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md): the manual Code Mode setup.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 1-337\n1: # Install Skilled\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: This guide installs Skilled and then sets it up in your own project repositories. Section 2 installs and checks a Skilled checkout. Sections 3 and 4 bring that checkout into a project, by linking it or by copying it in.\n6: \n7: From section 3 on, you run each step as a `/doctor` command from the `system-skilled-doctor` skill. A command that writes shows you a plan first and waits for your yes.\n8: \n9: ### Link or Copy\n10: \n11: You can set up a project in one of two ways. Pick one per project.\n12: \n13: | | Link | Copy |\n14: | --- | --- | --- |\n15: | **How it works** | Your project links to your Skilled checkout | Your project commits its own copy of Skilled |\n16: | **Updates** | One `git pull` in the checkout updates every linked project | You re-pin the copy: move it from the commit it came from to a newer one |\n17: | **Your changes** | Live in your project's own files, next to the links | Live in an overlay folder that goes back on the copy after each update |\n18: | **Teammates** | Each one keeps their own Skilled checkout | Everyone gets Skilled from the project repo |\n19: | **Choose it when** | You work alone, or every teammate keeps a checkout | The team needs one pinned version, or you change Skilled's own files |\n20: \n21: Linking is simpler. Choose a copy only when you need one of its two reasons.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. INSTALL A SKILLED CHECKOUT\n26: \n27: ### Prerequisites\n28: \n29: You need Node.js 24, `npm`, `git` and a POSIX shell. Node 24 is the one version every part of the framework accepts.\n30: \n31: ### Clone and Build\n32: \n33: Clone the repository and step into it:\n34: \n35: ```bash\n36: git clone https://github.com/MichelKerkmeester/skilled-agent-harness_spec-driven-loops.git\n37: cd skilled-agent-harness_spec-driven-loops\n38: ```\n39: \n40: Build the Spec Kit first. The runtimes' session hooks load this build.\n41: \n42: ```bash\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n45: ```\n46: \n47: Then build the Skill Advisor. Its build uses the Spec Kit's TypeScript compiler, so it comes second. The last command checks the advisor's CLI. `list-tools` answers offline, with no daemon running.\n48: \n49: ```bash\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: ### Add Code Mode\n72: \n73: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n74: \n75: ```\n76: /doctor:mcp install\n77: ```\n78: \n79: It installs the dependencies and builds Code Mode when its `dist` is missing or stale. It configures the `.utcp_config.json` manuals. It registers Code Mode in the seven project config files, two of them for Claude. Each write waits for its own approval. Add `--runtime <name>` to register one runtime only: `opencode`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `pi` or `devin`.\n80: \n81: To check Code Mode later, run `/doctor:mcp debug`. It reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and `--fix` adds guided repair. Provider keys live in `.env`, which only Code Mode reads. Section 1 of [`.env.example`](.env.example) lists them. An agent cannot read that file: the [dotenv guard](.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/README.md) refuses it on every runtime and offers key names or a fingerprint instead. The [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md) covers the manual steps.\n82: \n83: ### Git Hooks\n84: \n85: The first AI session installs the repository's git hooks. The root README's [Git Hooks](README.md#git-hooks) section says what each hook blocks. `/doctor:git setup` checks the hooks and the sk-git settings.\n86: \n87: Your checkout is ready once `/doctor:setup` passes. Run `/doctor:setup` again whenever something looks wrong. To use Skilled in a project of your own, pick a way in below.\n88: \n89: ---\n90: \n91: ## 3. LINK IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n92: \n93: ### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n94: \n95: Open your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n96: \n97: ```\n98: /doctor:install\n99: ```\n100: \n101: It asks four questions in one prompt:\n102: \n103: 1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n104: 2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n105: 3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n106: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n107: \n108: <!-- readme-check\n109: allow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n110: -->\n111: \n112: The guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n113: \n114: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n115: \n116: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n117: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n118: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n119: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n120: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n121: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n122: | 5 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n123: \n124: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n125: \n126: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n127: \n128: ```\n129: /doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n130: ```\n131: \n132: Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n133: \n134: ### What Gets Linked\n135: \n136: - **Always:** `.skilled`.\n137: - **Per runtime:** `.claude` with `.mcp.json`, `.opencode`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.pi`.\n138: - **On request:** `--include` takes `repo-rules`, `github`, `utcp` or `env`. They add the `repo-rules` folder, `.github`, `.utcp_config.json` and `.env`.\n139: - **Secrets:** linking `.env` shares the checkout's secrets with every tool in the project. The plan warns you before you approve it.\n140: \n141: The link shape decides how each folder is linked:\n142: \n143: - **`whole`:** each folder becomes one link to the checkout where it can.\n144: - **`merge`:** the folder stays a real folder, and each entry inside it becomes its own link.\n145: - **`auto`:** picks per folder, as described below.\n146: \n147: With `auto`, a folder your project already has stays a real folder. Each entry inside it becomes its own link, and your own files there stay untouched.\n148: \n149: A folder your project lacks becomes one link. The exception is a folder that holds a link to a sibling folder, such as `.skilled` (its `specs` link) or `.claude` (its `skills` link). The engine builds that folder entry by entry instead.\n150: \n151: ### Keep the Links Out of Git\n152: \n153: Most links point at your machine's checkout, so never commit them. `link` writes an ignore line for each of those to `.git/info/exclude`. Git reads that file but never commits it. Pass `--ignore gitignore` to write `.gitignore` instead.\n154: \n155: One link is different. When your project has its own `specs/` folder, `.skilled/specs` links to it with a relative path. That link works on any machine, so it receives no ignore line and you can commit it.\n156: \n157: ### Undo a Link\n158: \n159: Each `link` run ends by printing its undo command:\n160: \n161: ```\n162: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs unlink --run <run dir> --dry-run\n163: ```\n164: \n165: `/doctor:symlink unlink --run <run dir>` does the same. Drop `--dry-run` to run it for real. Unlink removes only what that run created. It restores only what that run replaced, and it removes the run's ignore lines. After several `link` runs, undo the newest first.\n166: \n167: > **Context saves.** `/speckit:save` records your session's progress in the `specs/` folder of the repo you run it from. Run `/doctor:setup` and every save from your project, not from the checkout.\n168: \n169: ---\n170: \n171: ## 4. COPY IT INTO YOUR PROJECT\n172: \n173: A re-pin replaces your copy whole with a newer commit. A change you made to the copy would be lost, so each change lives in an overlay instead. An overlay is a file in your project's overlay folder. `/doctor:overlay` applies it on top of the copy.\n174: \n175: <!-- readme-check\n176: allow-ref overlay-manifest.json | the manifest inside the overlay folder of a project that copies Skilled in\n177: allow-ref skilled-overlays/overlay-manifest.json | the manifest path the engine names in its error, in a project that copies Skilled in\n178: allow-ref skilled-overlays/ | the overlay folder in a project that copies Skilled in, which this checkout does not ship\n179: allow-ref .skilled-overlays.json | the optional overlay folder setting in a project that copies Skilled in, which this checkout does not ship\n180: -->\n181: \n182: ### Step 1: Create the Copy\n183: \n184: Export `.skilled` and the runtime folders you use from one commit of your checkout:\n185: \n186: ```bash\n187: cd /path/to/skilled\n188: git archive <commit> .skilled .claude .opencode | tar -x -C /path/to/your-project\n189: ```\n190: \n191: Commit the result in your project. Note the commit you exported. That commit is your pin.\n192: \n193: ### Step 2: Create the Overlay Folder\n194: \n195: The engine looks for `skilled-overlays/` at the root of your project. To use another folder, add `.skilled-overlays.json` at the root, for example `{ \"overlayDir\": \"my-overlays\" }`.\n196: \n197: The folder holds `overlay-manifest.json` and your overlay files. This manifest replaces one upstream file and adds a folder of team commands:\n198: \n199: ```json\n200: {\n201:   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n202:   \"pin\": { \"upstream\": \"skilled\", \"commit\": \"<the commit you exported>\" },\n203:   \"layoutLinks\": [],\n204:   \"overlays\": [\n205:     {\n206:       \"id\": \"commit-template\",\n207:       \"scope\": \"file\",\n208:       \"source\": \"sk-git/commit-message-template.md\",\n209:       \"destination\": \".skilled/skills/sk-git/assets/commit-message-template.md\"\n210:     },\n211:     {\n212:       \"id\": \"team-commands\",\n213:       \"scope\": \"directory\",\n214:       \"source\": \"team-commands\",\n215:       \"destination\": \".skilled/commands/team\"\n216:     }\n217:   ],\n218:   \"regenerate\": [],\n219:   \"verifyGenerated\": []\n220: }\n221: ```\n222: \n223: - **`source`:** where your version lives, inside the overlay folder.\n224: - **`destination`:** the path in the copy that the overlay owns.\n225: \n226: Save your version of each file at its `source` path.\n227: \n228: ### Overlay Types\n229: \n230: | `scope` | What the overlay does |\n231: | --- | --- |\n232: | `file` | Replaces one file with your version |\n233: | `directory` | Keeps a folder equal to your folder |\n234: | `marked-section` | Keeps your block between two marker lines in an upstream file |\n235: | `json-entry` | Changes named keys in an upstream JSON file |\n236: | `skill-root` | Replaces a whole skill folder with yours |\n237: | `remove-root` | Removes named upstream paths from the copy |\n238: \n239: Most projects need only `file` and `directory`. The [overlays reference](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md) covers the rest, plus the optional `regenerate`, `verifyGenerated` and `repin` blocks.\n240: \n241: ### Step 3: Apply the Overlays\n242: \n243: Check what is out of sync:\n244: \n245: ```\n246: /doctor:overlay status\n247: ```\n248: \n249: A new overlay reads `overlay-edited`, because the copy does not have it yet. Apply it:\n250: \n251: ```\n252: /doctor:overlay apply\n253: ```\n254: \n255: `apply` shows the status report as its plan and writes after your yes. Run `status` again. It now ends with `RESULT: PASSED`. Commit the overlay folder and the copy together.\n256: \n257: Running `apply` a second time changes nothing.\n258: \n259: ### Change an Overlay\n260: \n261: Edit the file in the overlay folder, never in the copy. Then run `apply`.\n262: \n263: Someone may still edit the copy directly. `status` then reports the file as `live-edited`, and `apply` refuses to write. Move the edit into its overlay:\n264: \n265: ```\n266: /doctor:overlay apply --capture <path>\n267: ```\n268: \n269: An AI agent is stopped sooner. The `overlay-guard` hook refuses an agent's edit to a file an overlay owns. It names the overlay file to edit instead.\n270: \n271: ### Step 4: Re-Pin to a Newer Commit\n272: \n273: A re-pin moves your copy to a newer commit and applies your overlays again. It reads from your Skilled checkout, which must hold both your pin and the new commit:\n274: \n275: ```\n276: /doctor:overlay repin --upstream /path/to/skilled --to <new commit>\n277: ```\n278: \n279: 1. **It stages first.** It builds the result in a temporary folder and leaves your project alone. The report lists the paths it will copy and delete, any blocked overlays and any overlays that now equal upstream.\n280: 2. **You fix the report.** Update each blocked overlay to match the new upstream file. Remove each overlay that now equals upstream. Run the command again.\n281: 3. **You approve.** The live run backs up every path it touches. Then it copies, moves the pin and applies the overlays.\n282: 4. **It checks the result.** The run ends with `RESULT: PASSED` and the new pin in your manifest.\n283: \n284: A re-pin copies `.skilled` and the runtime folders. It never copies a root file such as `AGENTS.md`, so your project's version survives. Each upstream change it skips prints as a `not-copied` line. Copy those over by hand if you want them. A top-level link, such as `specs`, is skipped without a line.\n285: \n286: A re-pin refuses to start when someone edited a file in place that no overlay owns, because the new copy would erase that edit. The refusal names the file. Move the edit into an overlay or add the path to the manifest's `repin.exclude` list. You can also restore the file from your pin.\n287: \n288: ### Undo a Re-Pin\n289: \n290: Each live run saves a backup in `skilled-overlays/repin-runs/<run-id>/` and prints the run id. Undo it with:\n291: \n292: ```\n293: /doctor:overlay repin --rollback <run-id>\n294: ```\n295: \n296: Rollback restores every backed-up file byte for byte. It removes the files the run added and sets the old pin back. Run `/doctor:overlay status` afterwards to confirm.\n297: \n298: ### Bring an Existing Overlay Folder\n299: \n300: Already keep overlays with a script of your own? The engine reads the same manifest and state files, so the folder stays where it is. Name it in `.skilled-overlays.json` and run `status`. Each line names its fix. The overlays reference has the full [adoption steps](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md#6-adopting-the-engine-with-existing-overlays).\n301: \n302: ---\n303: \n304: ## 5. KEEP IT HEALTHY\n305: \n306: | When | Linked project | Copied project |\n307: | --- | --- | --- |\n308: | **After a `git pull` in the checkout** | Run `/doctor:symlink check --root <dir>`. Run `link` again if it lists missing entries | No action until you re-pin |\n309: | **To adopt a new Skilled release** | The `git pull` already adopted it | Run `/doctor:overlay repin` |\n310: | **When something looks wrong** | Run `/doctor:setup` in your project | Run `/doctor:overlay status`, then `/doctor:setup` |\n311: | **To find the right command** | Run `/doctor:helper` and describe the problem | Same as linked |\n312: \n313: ---\n314: \n315: ## 6. TROUBLESHOOTING\n316: \n317: | You see | Cause | Fix |\n318: | --- | --- | --- |\n319: | `partial-merge` in `/doctor:symlink check` | The checkout gained entries since your last `link` | Run `link` again |\n320: | `no overlay manifest at skilled-overlays/overlay-manifest.json` | The engine found no overlay folder | Create one (section 4, step 2), or name yours in `.skilled-overlays.json` |\n321: | `overlay-edited` | An overlay changed and the copy lags behind | Run `/doctor:overlay apply` |\n322: | `live-edited` | Someone edited the copy directly | Run `/doctor:overlay apply --capture <path>` |\n323: | `both-changed` | The overlay and the copy both changed since the last apply | Read both, update the overlay by hand and run `status` again |\n324: | `upstream-moved` | The pin moved, and the file matches neither the old copy nor your overlay | Update the overlay to fit the new upstream file and run `status` again |\n325: | `refusing to inspect a protected path` | An overlay walks a file with `token` in its name | Add that file to the overlay's `protectedPaths`, as the line says |\n326: | `refuse: unowned <path> differs from the old pin` | Someone edited a file in place that no overlay owns | Move the edit into an overlay, or restore the file from your pin |\n327: | A held `.build-lock` | Another `apply` is running, or one crashed | Once no run is active, delete the lock file the message names |\n328: \n329: ---\n330: \n331: ## 7. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n332: \n333: - [system-skilled-doctor README](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/README.md): every doctor command in this guide.\n334: - [Overlays reference](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/references/overlays.md): sync states, refusals, re-pins and adoption in full.\n335: - [overlay-guard README](.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/README.md): the hook that protects overlay-owned files.\n336: - [Root README](README.md): what Skilled is and what each part does.\n337: - [Code Mode install guide](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/INSTALL-GUIDE.md): the manual Code Mode setup."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538522752,"end":1794538523547}}}}
