{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538567486,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d5741d002XW96IZ3y28Bor0","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d4ecc7001pKsUO1PlYJIv0o","type":"tool","id":"call_679f0268b4644c20b8b9bca6","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt, lines 1-204\n1: # /doctor:install Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:install`: the argument failure, the build check, the install prompt, the symlink check, the ordered steps, the caveat line, result templates and next-step text. The command router owns flag binding and asset loading. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: This command only reads. Every step that writes is printed with its exact command, and the operator runs it.\n6: \n7: Write for someone who has just cloned Skilled and wants it in their own project: plain words, short sentences, one thing at a time.\n8: \n9: ## 1. Argument Failure\n10: \n11: An unknown argument fails before any workflow YAML loads and prints the wording below with the bracketed parts filled in, then ends with the status line. Nothing is read and nothing is changed.\n12: \n13: | Situation | Wording |\n14: |-----------|---------|\n15: | A flag other than `--root <dir>`, `--runtimes <list>` and `--json` | `Unknown argument: [argument]` then `/doctor:install takes --root <dir>, --runtimes <list> and --json, or list and ?.` then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n16: | `--root` or `--runtimes` with no value after it | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n17: | A second positional token | The same two lines, then `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_argument\"` |\n18: \n19: `list`, `?` and `menu` as the whole argument print the steps in section 6, with `<dir>`, `<list>` and `<shape>` left as they stand, then stop. They load no workflow and inspect nothing.\n20: \n21: ## 2. The Build Check\n22: \n23: The Skilled checkout is the repository this command runs in. The runtimes load two builds from it, so check both before anything is planned.\n24: \n25: | Build | Check, run from the checkout root | Built when |\n26: |-------|-----------------------------------|------------|\n27: | Spec Kit | `test -d .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist && test -f .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` | exit 0 |\n28: | Skill Advisor | `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json` | exit 0 |\n29: \n30: Render both lines, then carry on either way: a missing build never stops the guide.\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: DOCTOR INSTALL — BUILDS\n34: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n35: Spec Kit build: [found at .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist and runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js | missing]\n36: Advisor CLI: [answers list-tools | missing or not built]\n37: ```\n38: \n39: A missing build becomes step 0 of the checklist. Step 0 carries the README's build commands word for word:\n40: \n41: ```bash\n42: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit install\n43: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build\n44: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n45: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Step 0 runs from the Skilled checkout. Its why line is: `Why: the session hooks and the advisor read these builds, so nothing else works until they are there.` It has no mutation class because no doctor route owns it.\n49: \n50: ## 3. The Install Prompt\n51: \n52: Ask every answer that is still missing in one prompt, then wait. This follows the consolidated question protocol. Questions 1 and 2 are dropped when `--root` and `--runtimes` were passed. The link shape and the instruction choice have no flag, so they are always in the prompt.\n53: \n54: ```text\n55: Where should Skilled go? Answer any or all in one reply, for example \"/Users/me/code/my-app, claude and codex, auto, embed\".\n56: \n57: 1) Target repo: the absolute path, for example /Users/me/code/my-app\n58: 2) Runtimes: claude, opencode, codex, cursor, devin, pi, or \"the ones already there\"\n59: 3) Link shape: auto / whole / merge   (auto unless a real folder already sits where a link would go)\n60: 4) Instruction file: embed / link   (embed keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md; link points AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md at the checkout's copies)\n61: ```\n62: \n63: The example carries all four answers so the shape of a full reply is visible. Never print a question the flags already answered.\n64: \n65: ## 4. Accepted Answers\n66: \n67: | Answer | Binds | Meaning |\n68: |--------|-------|---------|\n69: | An absolute path | `--root <dir>` | The project repo that receives the links. The path must exist and be a directory; the engine exits 2 and names it otherwise |\n70: | `claude`, `claude and codex`, `claude,opencode` | `--runtimes <list>` | The runtime folders to link, as a comma list |\n71: | `the ones already there`, empty, `any` | no `--runtimes` | The engine keeps the runtimes its own detection finds in the root, and always links `.skilled` |\n72: | `auto` | `--mode auto` | Whole link where the path is free, merge where a real folder is in the way. The one to pick |\n73: | `whole` | `--mode whole` | One link per entry, refused where a real folder exists |\n74: | `merge` | `--mode merge` | A real folder whose children are links. A local file already in the folder is kept and reported, never overwritten |\n75: | `embed` | step 2 stays | The repo keeps its own `AGENTS.md` and the shipped sections are refreshed into it |\n76: | `link` | step 1 gains `--link-instructions`, step 2 is dropped | `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` become links into the checkout |\n77: \n78: A runtime name outside the seven, a shape outside the three, or an instruction word outside the two is not guessed. Ask that one question again with the accepted values. When the engine refuses a root, show its `ERROR:` line as it printed and ask question 1 again.\n79: \n80: ## 5. The Symlink Check\n81: \n82: Run `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root <dir> [--runtimes <list>] [--link-instructions]` once, in place and read-only, then render its entry lines as they print:\n83: \n84: ```text\n85: DOCTOR INSTALL — WHAT IS ALREADY THERE\n86: Root: [the target repo]\n87: [the engine's entry lines, verbatim, with its indented detail lines and its repo-level warnings]\n88: ```\n89: \n90: Do not re-sort the lines, re-word a status or sum them into a verdict. A `missing` line is work for step 1, not a failure, and the check still exits 0 for it. The check exits 1 only on drift: a broken or foreign link, including a broken link inside a merged folder, a missing source or a tracked absolute link. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Add `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n91: \n92: | Status | What it means for this install |\n93: |--------|-------------------------------|\n94: | `linked-whole` | Already a link into the checkout. Step 1 has nothing to do for it |\n95: | `linked-merge` | A real folder whose children are links. Nothing to do |\n96: | `partial-merge` | A real folder missing some links. Step 1 fills the gaps and never deletes a local file |\n97: | `missing` | Not there yet. Step 1 creates it |\n98: | `broken` | A link whose target is gone. Step 1 replaces it |\n99: | `foreign-link` | A link that points somewhere else. Left alone, and the engine refuses to touch it |\n100: | `local` | A real file or folder of the repo's own. Left alone |\n101: | `source-missing` | The checkout has no such path. Nothing is planned |\n102: \n103: ## 6. The Ordered Steps\n104: \n105: This is the checklist, and it is also what `list`, `?` and `menu` print. Each step carries its exact command, its class and one line of why.\n106: \n107: The class column is the manifest's `mutating` value for the route that owns the printed command, verbatim, so it is read from the route table and never guessed. A command with no route of its own prints `n/a`.\n108: \n109: ```text\n110: 1) /doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode <shape>   [class]\n111:    Why: creates the links. It shows a plan first and asks before it writes.\n112: \n113: 2) /doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>   [class]\n114:    Why: keeps the repo's own AGENTS.md and refreshes the shipped sections into it. Dropped when the instruction choice is link.\n115: \n116: 3) /doctor:mcp install   [class]\n117:    Why: builds and registers Code Mode. Run it from the Skilled checkout.\n118: \n119: 4) /doctor:git setup   [class]\n120:    Why: checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, and names the repair for each one that is off. Run it from the target repo.\n121: \n122: 5) /doctor:skill-advisor embedder   [class]\n123:    Why: sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server. Run it from the target repo.\n124: \n125: 6) /doctor:setup   [class]\n126:    Why: confirms the result. Run it from the target repo.\n127: ```\n128: \n129: Run them in this order. Step 1 takes `--link-instructions` when the instruction choice is `link`.\n130: \n131: When the workflow renders the checklist after the check, print this header above the steps:\n132: \n133: ```text\n134: DOCTOR INSTALL — [the target repo]\n135: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n136: Runtimes: [the runtime list]   Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]   Instruction file: [embed|link]\n137: ```\n138: \n139: A printed step is handed back, never run: each writing command shows its own plan, asks its own yes and writes under its own gate. This command adds no argument to a printed command beyond the values the operator gave.\n140: \n141: ## 7. The Caveat Line\n142: \n143: Print this one line word for word after the steps, on every run, before the result. It is fixed: do not shorten it and do not rewrite it in the operator's words.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: context saves land in the target repo's own specs/ when they run from inside it, so run /doctor:setup and later saves from inside the target repo, not from the Skilled checkout.\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## 8. Result Templates\n150: \n151: ### Summary\n152: \n153: ```text\n154: DOCTOR INSTALL RESULT\n155: Source: [the Skilled checkout]\n156: Root: [the target repo]\n157: Runtimes: [the runtime list]\n158: Link shape: [auto|whole|merge]\n159: Instruction file: [embed|link]\n160: Builds: [both found | missing: <which>, printed as step 0]\n161: Already there: [n] linked, [n] missing, [n] to repair\n162: Steps: [n] printed, [n] of them write\n163: Next: run step 1 from the Skilled checkout, then the rest in order\n164: STATUS=OK STEPS=[n]\n165: ```\n166: \n167: ### JSON\n168: \n169: `--json` prints one JSON object and nothing else: no build lines, no steps, no caveat, no header.\n170: \n171: | Key | Value |\n172: |-----|-------|\n173: | `source` | The Skilled checkout's absolute path |\n174: | `root` | The target repo's absolute path |\n175: | `runtimes` | The runtime names, as strings |\n176: | `builds` | One entry per probe in section 2, true or false |\n177: | `symlink_check` | The engine's `check --json` object, unchanged |\n178: | `steps` | One object per printed step: `order`, `command`, `mutating`, `why` |\n179: \n180: ### Failure Summary\n181: \n182: ```text\n183: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n184: Target: guide\n185: Step: [the step that failed]\n186: Error: [message]\n187: Next: [the accepted invocation, or the command to rerun]\n188: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## 9. Troubleshooting Display\n192: \n193: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n194: |-----------|------------------|\n195: | The engine exits 2 | Bad invocation or a refused root. Its first line names the flag or the path. Fix that one thing and rerun the same command |\n196: | The root is the checkout, sits inside it, or holds it | The engine refuses it, because linking a checkout into itself would loop. Name the project repo that should receive the links |\n197: | A build is missing | Run the four `npm` commands in section 2 from the checkout, then rerun this guide. They also print as step 0 |\n198: | A step prints `n/a` as its class | That printed command has no route in the manifest yet. The command still works; only its class is unknown |\n199: | A line reads `local` or `foreign-link` | Left alone on purpose. Move that file or link yourself, or bring it under step 1's shape, and rerun the guide |\n200: | Only the steps are wanted | `list` prints them with no build check and no inspection |\n201: | A saved session lands in the checkout's `specs/` | The save ran from the Skilled checkout. Run it again from inside the target repo, as the caveat in section 7 says |\n202: | The project copies Skilled in instead of linking it | This guide covers linking only. A copy that keeps its own changes keeps them as overlays: run `/doctor:overlay status --root <copy>`, and see the overlays reference in `system-skilled-doctor` for adopting the engine when the project already has its own overlay folder |\n203: \n204: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538566685,"end":1794538567486}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538567495,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d575de001l6FMkX1zCekp3Q","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d4ecc7001pKsUO1PlYJIv0o","type":"tool","id":"call_fd7dfeb60f68448295acc0da","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-300\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Set up meaning matching            (embedder for commands, asks before any change)\n17:    6) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n18:    7) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n19:    H) Help me decide\n20:    X) Cancel\n21: ```\n22: \n23: Accepted answers:\n24: \n25: | Answer | Result |\n26: |--------|--------|\n27: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n28: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n29: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n30: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n31: | `5` | target = `embedder` |\n32: | `6` | target = `skill-budget` |\n33: | `7` | target = `parent-skill` |\n34: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n35: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n36: \n37: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n38: \n39: ### Help Block\n40: \n41: ```text\n42: Pick by symptom:\n43: \n44:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n45:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n46:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n47:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n48:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n49:    A plain request never gets its command offered      -> 5  Meaning matching setup\n50:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 6  Description budget\n51:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 7  Parent-skill structure\n52: \n53: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n54:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n55:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n56:    Description budget (6) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n57: \n58: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: ### Unknown Target Failure\n62: \n63: ```text\n64: Unknown target: [target]\n65: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, embedder, skill-budget, parent-skill\n66: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n67: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n68: ```\n69: \n70: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n71: \n72: ```text\n73: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n74: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n75: ```\n76: \n77: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n78: \n79: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n80: \n81: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n82: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n83: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n84: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n85: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n86: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n87: | `embedder` | `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | mutates | Set up meaning matching for commands: probe Ollama and the model, show each step's cost and undo, and change nothing before a yes |\n88: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n89: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n90: \n91: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n92: \n93: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n94: \n95: ### Tune Scope\n96: \n97: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n98: \n99: ```text\n100: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n101:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n102:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n103:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n104:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n105: ```\n106: \n107: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n108: \n109: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n110: \n111: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n112: \n113: ### Router-Reach Scope\n114: \n115: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n116: \n117: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n118: \n119: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n120: \n121: ```text\n122: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n123: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n124: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n125: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n126: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n127: Will run:\n128:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n129:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n130: ```\n131: \n132: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n133: \n134: Otherwise ask:\n135: \n136: ```text\n137: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n138: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n139: ```\n140: \n141: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n142: \n143: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n147: Target: [target]\n148: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n149: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n150: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n151: Setup values: [key=value list]\n152: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n153: Next: load workflow YAML\n154: ```\n155: \n156: ## 6. Result Templates\n157: \n158: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n159: \n160: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n161: \n162: ```text\n163: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n164: Target: [target]\n165: Workflow: [yaml]\n166: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n167: Mutation class: read-only\n168: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n169: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n170: STATUS=[status]\n171: ```\n172: \n173: ### Mutating Target Summary\n174: \n175: ```text\n176: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n177: Target: [target]\n178: Workflow: [yaml]\n179: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n180: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n181: Files modified: [list or none]\n182: Verification: [checks run and result]\n183: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n184: STATUS=[status]\n185: ```\n186: \n187: ### Failure Summary\n188: \n189: ```text\n190: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n191: Target: [target]\n192: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n193: Error: [message]\n194: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n195: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n196: ```\n197: \n198: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n199: \n200: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n201: |-----------|------------------|\n202: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n203: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n204: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n205: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n206: \n207: ## 8. Embedder Setup Presentation\n208: \n209: Render these blocks for `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. The probe runs first and changes nothing. Every value is printed as the probe or the cost script returned it, and an unread value stays unread.\n210: \n211: ### Probe Dashboard\n212: \n213: Render after the read-only probe and before the plan.\n214: \n215: ```text\n216: EMBEDDER SETUP PROBE\n217: Ollama binary: [present at <path>|missing]\n218: Server: [answering at <url>, version <version>|absent at <url>]\n219: Model: [nomic-embed-text:v1.5 present, <size> on disk|missing]\n220: Advisor daemon: [present|absent]\n221: Active embedder: [<backend> <model>|none|unread, the daemon is absent]\n222: Command vectors: [<embedded> of <total>|unread, the daemon is absent]\n223: Semantic lane: [enabled|off ([disabledReason])|unread, the daemon is absent]\n224: ```\n225: \n226: A missing binary, an absent server and a missing model are findings, not failures of the route. An exit 75 from `advisor_status` means the daemon is absent, so the active embedder, the command vectors and the lane state stay `unread`.\n227: \n228: ### Plan Table\n229: \n230: Render one row per missing step, in dependency order. A step the probe found present is not listed and is not run. Each cost comes from `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` or, when the cost script cannot run, from the install guide with a note that the live measurement was unavailable.\n231: \n232: ```text\n233: EMBEDDER SETUP PLAN\n234: Missing: [comma-separated steps, or none]\n235: \n236: | Step | Cost | Undo |\n237: |------|------|------|\n238: | Install Ollama (printed only, never run by this route) | [the install guide's cost] | [the package manager's uninstall command] |\n239: | Start ollama serve in the background | [.memory.serveRssKb from the cost script] resident | Stop the pid this run started |\n240: | Pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5 | [.model.sizeBytes from the cost script] on disk | ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5 |\n241: | Run skill_graph_scan to write the command vectors | [the scan's own runtime] plus [.warm.medianMs from the cost script] per embedded prompt | None, the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it |\n242: \n243: Will run after approval:\n244:    [the listed steps, in dependency order, or none]\n245: ```\n246: \n247: When the probe found no missing step, skip the table and render the final result as already set up.\n248: \n249: ### Approval Prompt\n250: \n251: Ask once, after the plan is on screen. Nothing is pulled, started or written before the answer, and approve is the only answer that proceeds.\n252: \n253: ```text\n254: Set up meaning matching now? Only the steps in the plan run.\n255: Steps:\n256:    [one line per approved step with its cost]\n257: Writes: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\n258: Never: an Ollama install or upgrade, a model the plan did not list, a model removal, a second server\n259: Reply approve to continue, or no to cancel.\n260: ```\n261: \n262: Anything other than approve renders the cancelled result and stops.\n263: \n264: ```text\n265: EMBEDDER SETUP CANCELLED\n266: Nothing was pulled, started or written.\n267: Next: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n268: STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n269: ```\n270: \n271: ### Dry-Run Result\n272: \n273: With `--dry-run`, stop after the plan, before the approval, and render this block.\n274: \n275: ```text\n276: EMBEDDER SETUP DRY RUN\n277: [the probe dashboard]\n278: [the plan table, with each missing step's cost and undo]\n279: \n280: Dry run: nothing was pulled, started or written.\n281: STATUS=OK\n282: ```\n283: \n284: ### Final Result\n285: \n286: Render after the post-scan probe. When the probe found nothing missing, render the same block from the probe values, ask nothing and run nothing.\n287: \n288: ```text\n289: EMBEDDER SETUP RESULT\n290: Server: [answering at <url>, version <version>|absent at <url>]\n291: Model: [nomic-embed-text:v1.5, <size> on disk|missing]\n292: Command vectors: [<embedded> of <total>|0 of <total>]\n293: Semantic lane: [enabled|off ([disabledReason])]\n294: Next: [none|restart the advisor daemon, the active embedder is resolved at startup|the repair the failed check names]\n295: STATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n296: ```\n297: \n298: Report `STATUS=OK` only when the lane is enabled and the embedded count is above zero. Otherwise report `STATUS=FAIL` and name the check that did not pass. When the active embedder is null, name a daemon restart, then rerun the probe.\n299: \n300: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-300\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Set up meaning matching            (embedder for commands, asks before any change)\n17:    6) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n18:    7) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n19:    H) Help me decide\n20:    X) Cancel\n21: ```\n22: \n23: Accepted answers:\n24: \n25: | Answer | Result |\n26: |--------|--------|\n27: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n28: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n29: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n30: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n31: | `5` | target = `embedder` |\n32: | `6` | target = `skill-budget` |\n33: | `7` | target = `parent-skill` |\n34: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n35: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n36: \n37: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n38: \n39: ### Help Block\n40: \n41: ```text\n42: Pick by symptom:\n43: \n44:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n45:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n46:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n47:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n48:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n49:    A plain request never gets its command offered      -> 5  Meaning matching setup\n50:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 6  Description budget\n51:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 7  Parent-skill structure\n52: \n53: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n54:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n55:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n56:    Description budget (6) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n57: \n58: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: ### Unknown Target Failure\n62: \n63: ```text\n64: Unknown target: [target]\n65: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, embedder, skill-budget, parent-skill\n66: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n67: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n68: ```\n69: \n70: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n71: \n72: ```text\n73: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n74: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n75: ```\n76: \n77: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n78: \n79: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n80: \n81: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n82: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n83: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n84: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n85: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n86: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n87: | `embedder` | `doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` | mutates | Set up meaning matching for commands: probe Ollama and the model, show each step's cost and undo, and change nothing before a yes |\n88: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n89: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n90: \n91: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n92: \n93: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n94: \n95: ### Tune Scope\n96: \n97: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n98: \n99: ```text\n100: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n101:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n102:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n103:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n104:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n105: ```\n106: \n107: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n108: \n109: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n110: \n111: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n112: \n113: ### Router-Reach Scope\n114: \n115: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n116: \n117: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n118: \n119: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n120: \n121: ```text\n122: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n123: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n124: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n125: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n126: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n127: Will run:\n128:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n129:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n130: ```\n131: \n132: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n133: \n134: Otherwise ask:\n135: \n136: ```text\n137: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n138: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n139: ```\n140: \n141: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n142: \n143: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n144: \n145: ```text\n146: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n147: Target: [target]\n148: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n149: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n150: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n151: Setup values: [key=value list]\n152: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n153: Next: load workflow YAML\n154: ```\n155: \n156: ## 6. Result Templates\n157: \n158: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n159: \n160: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n161: \n162: ```text\n163: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n164: Target: [target]\n165: Workflow: [yaml]\n166: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n167: Mutation class: read-only\n168: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n169: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n170: STATUS=[status]\n171: ```\n172: \n173: ### Mutating Target Summary\n174: \n175: ```text\n176: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n177: Target: [target]\n178: Workflow: [yaml]\n179: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n180: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n181: Files modified: [list or none]\n182: Verification: [checks run and result]\n183: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n184: STATUS=[status]\n185: ```\n186: \n187: ### Failure Summary\n188: \n189: ```text\n190: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n191: Target: [target]\n192: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n193: Error: [message]\n194: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n195: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n196: ```\n197: \n198: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n199: \n200: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n201: |-----------|------------------|\n202: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n203: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n204: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n205: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n206: \n207: ## 8. Embedder Setup Presentation\n208: \n209: Render these blocks for `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder`. The probe runs first and changes nothing. Every value is printed as the probe or the cost script returned it, and an unread value stays unread.\n210: \n211: ### Probe Dashboard\n212: \n213: Render after the read-only probe and before the plan.\n214: \n215: ```text\n216: EMBEDDER SETUP PROBE\n217: Ollama binary: [present at <path>|missing]\n218: Server: [answering at <url>, version <version>|absent at <url>]\n219: Model: [nomic-embed-text:v1.5 present, <size> on disk|missing]\n220: Advisor daemon: [present|absent]\n221: Active embedder: [<backend> <model>|none|unread, the daemon is absent]\n222: Command vectors: [<embedded> of <total>|unread, the daemon is absent]\n223: Semantic lane: [enabled|off ([disabledReason])|unread, the daemon is absent]\n224: ```\n225: \n226: A missing binary, an absent server and a missing model are findings, not failures of the route. An exit 75 from `advisor_status` means the daemon is absent, so the active embedder, the command vectors and the lane state stay `unread`.\n227: \n228: ### Plan Table\n229: \n230: Render one row per missing step, in dependency order. A step the probe found present is not listed and is not run. Each cost comes from `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` or, when the cost script cannot run, from the install guide with a note that the live measurement was unavailable.\n231: \n232: ```text\n233: EMBEDDER SETUP PLAN\n234: Missing: [comma-separated steps, or none]\n235: \n236: | Step | Cost | Undo |\n237: |------|------|------|\n238: | Install Ollama (printed only, never run by this route) | [the install guide's cost] | [the package manager's uninstall command] |\n239: | Start ollama serve in the background | [.memory.serveRssKb from the cost script] resident | Stop the pid this run started |\n240: | Pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5 | [.model.sizeBytes from the cost script] on disk | ollama rm nomic-embed-text:v1.5 |\n241: | Run skill_graph_scan to write the command vectors | [the scan's own runtime] plus [.warm.medianMs from the cost script] per embedded prompt | None, the database is derived state and a rerun rewrites it |\n242: \n243: Will run after approval:\n244:    [the listed steps, in dependency order, or none]\n245: ```\n246: \n247: When the probe found no missing step, skip the table and render the final result as already set up.\n248: \n249: ### Approval Prompt\n250: \n251: Ask once, after the plan is on screen. Nothing is pulled, started or written before the answer, and approve is the only answer that proceeds.\n252: \n253: ```text\n254: Set up meaning matching now? Only the steps in the plan run.\n255: Steps:\n256:    [one line per approved step with its cost]\n257: Writes: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite, through skill_graph_scan only\n258: Never: an Ollama install or upgrade, a model the plan did not list, a model removal, a second server\n259: Reply approve to continue, or no to cancel.\n260: ```\n261: \n262: Anything other than approve renders the cancelled result and stops.\n263: \n264: ```text\n265: EMBEDDER SETUP CANCELLED\n266: Nothing was pulled, started or written.\n267: Next: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n268: STATUS=CANCELLED ACTION=cancelled\n269: ```\n270: \n271: ### Dry-Run Result\n272: \n273: With `--dry-run`, stop after the plan, before the approval, and render this block.\n274: \n275: ```text\n276: EMBEDDER SETUP DRY RUN\n277: [the probe dashboard]\n278: [the plan table, with each missing step's cost and undo]\n279: \n280: Dry run: nothing was pulled, started or written.\n281: STATUS=OK\n282: ```\n283: \n284: ### Final Result\n285: \n286: Render after the post-scan probe. When the probe found nothing missing, render the same block from the probe values, ask nothing and run nothing.\n287: \n288: ```text\n289: EMBEDDER SETUP RESULT\n290: Server: [answering at <url>, version <version>|absent at <url>]\n291: Model: [nomic-embed-text:v1.5, <size> on disk|missing]\n292: Command vectors: [<embedded> of <total>|0 of <total>]\n293: Semantic lane: [enabled|off ([disabledReason])]\n294: Next: [none|restart the advisor daemon, the active embedder is resolved at startup|the repair the failed check names]\n295: STATUS=[OK|FAIL]\n296: ```\n297: \n298: Report `STATUS=OK` only when the lane is enabled and the embedded count is above zero. Otherwise report `STATUS=FAIL` and name the check that did not pass. When the active embedder is null, name a daemon restart, then rerun the probe.\n299: \n300: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538567134,"end":1794538567495}}}}
