{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794538764551,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"id":"prt_1d2d87907001SCwLSnVDD2pIka","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d86ec0001sBB2bvtIpsGK4o","type":"step-start","snapshot":"7e7ee18bdb06276f04809e4aeb8e61962341e242"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538769397,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d8797d001lnzMO4IseTzYAe","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d86ec0001sBB2bvtIpsGK4o","type":"tool","id":"call_662f5a4aa70644a281189c22","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n\n### Meaning Matching for Commands\n\nUntil a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n\nRun the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n\n```\n/doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n```\n\nIt probes Ollama, the server and the model first, and changes nothing. It then lists each missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks before it acts. Only `approve` proceeds. It pulls the model it listed, starts `ollama serve` in the background and runs `skill_graph_scan` to write a vector for every command entry. It never installs or upgrades Ollama. When Ollama is missing, the plan prints the install command for you to run.\n\nMeasured on 2026-11-13 with Ollama 0.40.15:\n\n| What it costs | Measured |\n| --- | --- |\n| Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes |\n| Memory while `ollama serve` is idle | 25776 KB resident |\n| Memory while the model is loaded | 32208 KB for the server plus 279520 KB for the model runner |\n| Unload when idle | after five idle minutes without a request |\n| Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n| Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n\nMeaning matching is optional. A no at the prompt changes nothing. The install keeps working on phrases alone, and each recommendation that ran without a prompt vector carries `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` in its `warnings`.\n\n### Add Code Mode","oldString":"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n\n### Add Code Mode","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md"},"output":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md","patch":"Index: INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n===================================================================\n--- INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n+++ INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n@@ -67,8 +67,33 @@\n DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n \n Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n \n+### Meaning Matching for Commands\n+\n+Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n+\n+Run the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n+\n+```\n+/doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n+```\n+\n+It probes Ollama, the server and the model first, and changes nothing. It then lists each missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks before it acts. Only `approve` proceeds. It pulls the model it listed, starts `ollama serve` in the background and runs `skill_graph_scan` to write a vector for every command entry. It never installs or upgrades Ollama. When Ollama is missing, the plan prints the install command for you to run.\n+\n+Measured on 2026-11-13 with Ollama 0.40.15:\n+\n+| What it costs | Measured |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes |\n+| Memory while `ollama serve` is idle | 25776 KB resident |\n+| Memory while the model is loaded | 32208 KB for the server plus 279520 KB for the model runner |\n+| Unload when idle | after five idle minutes without a request |\n+| Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n+| Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n+\n+Meaning matching is optional. A no at the prompt changes nothing. The install keeps working on phrases alone, and each recommendation that ran without a prompt vector carries `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` in its `warnings`.\n+\n ### Add Code Mode\n \n Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n \n","status":"modified","additions":25,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\\n\\n### Meaning Matching for Commands\\n\\nUntil a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\\n\\nRun the setup from the repository you are setting up:\\n\\n```\\n/doctor:skill-advisor embedder\\n```\\n\\nIt probes Ollama, the server and the model first, and changes nothing. It then lists each missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks before it acts. Only `approve` proceeds. It pulls the model it listed, starts `ollama serve` in the background and runs `skill_graph_scan` to write a vector for every command entry. It never installs or upgrades Ollama. When Ollama is missing, the plan prints the install command for you to run.\\n\\nMeasured on 2026-11-13 with Ollama 0.40.15:\\n\\n| What it costs | Measured |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes |\\n| Memory while `ollama serve` is idle | 25776 KB resident |\\n| Memory while the model is loaded | 32208 KB for the server plus 279520 KB for the model runner |\\n| Unload when idle | after five idle minutes without a request |\\n| Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\\n| Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\\n\\nMeaning matching is optional. A no at the prompt changes nothing. The install keeps working on phrases alone, and each recommendation that ran without a prompt vector carries `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` in its `warnings`.\\n\\n### Add Code Mode\",\"oldString\":\"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\\n\\n### Add Code Mode\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538764669,"end":1794538769397}}}}
