{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538790073,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d8daaa001NFblEQqGaY9Ae8","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d8c69e001WF4C9ZWDcLdKwF","type":"tool","id":"call_745c1c2a365642f293954fd6","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md","offset":138,"limit":16},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 138-153\n138: \n139: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n140: \n141: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n142: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n143: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n144: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n145: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n146: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n147: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n148: | 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n149: \n150: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n151: \n152: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n153: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 154]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 138-153\n138: \n139: ### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n140: \n141: | Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n142: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n143: | 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n144: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n145: | 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n146: | 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n147: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n148: | 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n149: \n150: If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n151: \n152: ### Step 3: Check the Links\n153: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 154]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"offset\":138,\"limit\":16}"},"time":{"start":1794538789546,"end":1794538790073}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538790076,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2d8d8a7001uISVK7SgEAh3rz","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2d8c69e001WF4C9ZWDcLdKwF","type":"tool","id":"call_4f9a4b482a4d455ab279a348","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md","offset":55,"limit":45},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 55-99\n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n72: \n73: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n74: \n75: Run the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n76: \n77: ```\n78: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n79: ```\n80: \n81: It probes Ollama, the server and the model first, and changes nothing. It then lists each missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks before it acts. Only `approve` proceeds. It pulls the model it listed, starts `ollama serve` in the background and runs `skill_graph_scan` to write a vector for every command entry. It never installs or upgrades Ollama. When Ollama is missing, the plan prints the install command for you to run.\n82: \n83: Measured on 2026-11-13 with Ollama 0.40.15:\n84: \n85: | What it costs | Measured |\n86: | --- | --- |\n87: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes |\n88: | Memory while `ollama serve` is idle | 25776 KB resident |\n89: | Memory while the model is loaded | 32208 KB for the server plus 279520 KB for the model runner |\n90: | Unload when idle | after five idle minutes without a request |\n91: | Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n92: | Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n93: \n94: Meaning matching is optional. A no at the prompt changes nothing. The install keeps working on phrases alone, and each recommendation that ran without a prompt vector carries `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` in its `warnings`.\n95: \n96: ### Add Code Mode\n97: \n98: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n99: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 100]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 55-99\n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n72: \n73: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n74: \n75: Run the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n76: \n77: ```\n78: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n79: ```\n80: \n81: It probes Ollama, the server and the model first, and changes nothing. It then lists each missing step with its cost and its undo, and asks before it acts. Only `approve` proceeds. It pulls the model it listed, starts `ollama serve` in the background and runs `skill_graph_scan` to write a vector for every command entry. It never installs or upgrades Ollama. When Ollama is missing, the plan prints the install command for you to run.\n82: \n83: Measured on 2026-11-13 with Ollama 0.40.15:\n84: \n85: | What it costs | Measured |\n86: | --- | --- |\n87: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes |\n88: | Memory while `ollama serve` is idle | 25776 KB resident |\n89: | Memory while the model is loaded | 32208 KB for the server plus 279520 KB for the model runner |\n90: | Unload when idle | after five idle minutes without a request |\n91: | Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n92: | Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n93: \n94: Meaning matching is optional. A no at the prompt changes nothing. The install keeps working on phrases alone, and each recommendation that ran without a prompt vector carries `semantic_lane_off:<reason>` in its `warnings`.\n95: \n96: ### Add Code Mode\n97: \n98: Code Mode is the bridge your runtime uses to call external MCP tools. It builds separately from the two builds above. Run:\n99: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 100]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"offset\":55,\"limit\":45}"},"time":{"start":1794538789031,"end":1794538790076}}}}
