{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794538894222,"sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2da7081001wAU3GHq3QMG7O0","sessionID":"ses_e2d2be7e1ffejV5G44JLfXNvVv","messageID":"msg_1d2da6609001G4gkn4Zl7bhfSJ","type":"tool","id":"call_673e3bff9f4340b7834918ed","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"argparse|add_argument|INSTALL|glob|README\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/scripts/check_readme_references.py | head -30"},"output":"3:# COMPONENT: README REFERENCE CHECKER (SK-DOC)\n6:\"\"\"Check local README links, file references, inventories and command paths.\n8:Usage: python3 check_readme_references.py [--self-test] README.md [...]\n21:  resolves when the README's folder holds it at any depth.\n60:A reference resolves from the README folder, from the nearest folder above it\n63:folder above the README, from ``.skilled/skills/`` and, for a relative code\n64:span, from each folder below the README, where an importing file may sit; a\n74:span, such as ``graph-metadata.json``, that is not beside the README passes\n84:tracked, a path a hub README names per mode that every child mode folder (a\n90:move: the sk-code loaders refuse it. Every README in a run is asked about\n92:call that finds the READMEs kept inside an ignored folder, where the rule does\n97:README-level marker block. Each entry suppresses that exact token in that README\n112:import argparse\n117:import glob\n203:# An extensionless sibling name whose ignored state shows a README's folder is ignored as a whole.\n236:    # also resolves when the README's folder holds it at any depth.\n301:    return value in {\"README.md\", \"pre-commit\", \"package.json\"}\n388:    its entries sit in the README folder. A root line such as `lib/` must name a\n389:    folder that exists from the README folder or a folder above it, or be the\n390:    README folder's own name. A root that names no such folder is reported once,\n451:        # Name the entry from the README folder, so the git-ignored check asks\n713:    does not hold stays tied to the README folder, so a stale relative path is\n715:    `.git/hooks/` names a path git owns, which a README allows by marker.\n728:    \"\"\"Resolve a literal or glob from the README directory, safe root anchors and a skill folder.\"\"\"\n769:    \"\"\"Tell whether a hub README names a path that every child mode folder holds.\"\"\"\n779:    A git-ignored path is the fourth class; it is cleared for every README of a\n812:    \"\"\"Resolve one literal, glob or filename template from every candidate base.\"\"\"\n818:            matches = sorted(glob.glob(str(candidate_path), recursive=True)) if any(\n837:    Only a span that exists whole counts, from the README folder, each folder above\n904:    return folder.is_dir() and any(folder.glob(\"*.md\"))\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:# COMPONENT: README REFERENCE CHECKER (SK-DOC)\n6:\"\"\"Check local README links, file references, inventories and command paths.\n8:Usage: python3 check_readme_references.py [--self-test] README.md [...]\n21:  resolves when the README's folder holds it at any depth.\n60:A reference resolves from the README folder, from the nearest folder above it\n63:folder above the README, from ``.skilled/skills/`` and, for a relative code\n64:span, from each folder below the README, where an importing file may sit; a\n74:span, such as ``graph-metadata.json``, that is not beside the README passes\n84:tracked, a path a hub README names per mode that every child mode folder (a\n90:move: the sk-code loaders refuse it. Every README in a run is asked about\n92:call that finds the READMEs kept inside an ignored folder, where the rule does\n97:README-level marker block. Each entry suppresses that exact token in that README\n112:import argparse\n117:import glob\n203:# An extensionless sibling name whose ignored state shows a README's folder is ignored as a whole.\n236:    # also resolves when the README's folder holds it at any depth.\n301:    return value in {\"README.md\", \"pre-commit\", \"package.json\"}\n388:    its entries sit in the README folder. A root line such as `lib/` must name a\n389:    folder that exists from the README folder or a folder above it, or be the\n390:    README folder's own name. A root that names no such folder is reported once,\n451:        # Name the entry from the README folder, so the git-ignored check asks\n713:    does not hold stays tied to the README folder, so a stale relative path is\n715:    `.git/hooks/` names a path git owns, which a README allows by marker.\n728:    \"\"\"Resolve a literal or glob from the README directory, safe root anchors and a skill folder.\"\"\"\n769:    \"\"\"Tell whether a hub README names a path that every child mode folder holds.\"\"\"\n779:    A git-ignored path is the fourth class; it is cleared for every README of a\n812:    \"\"\"Resolve one literal, glob or filename template from every candidate base.\"\"\"\n818:            matches = sorted(glob.glob(str(candidate_path), recursive=True)) if any(\n837:    Only a span that exists whole counts, from the README folder, each folder above\n904:    return folder.is_dir() and any(folder.glob(\"*.md\"))\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"argparse|add_argument|INSTALL|glob|README\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/scripts/check_readme_references.py | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794538893442,"end":1794538894222}}}}
